// REQUIRES: gdb, lldb, host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %gopp build %S/Inputs/parambreak.gopp -o %t
// RUN: timeout 30 gdb -batch -nx -q -x %S/Inputs/parambreak.gdb %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GDB
// RUN: timeout 30 gdb -batch -nx -q -x %S/Inputs/parambreak-step.gdb %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GDBSTEP
// SPLIT: params-break 1/2
// P04.12 (every value at `opt 0` is right): `break f` stops where LLVM puts
// prologue_end, the first instruction with a line. The code that puts the
// parameters where their variables say they are (the stores into their
// slots, the variable a borrowed string or `[]T` pair is made into, the zero
// value of a named result) has no line, as in Clang, so it runs before that
// stop. Before the fix the stores had the declaration line and gdb showed
// `one (a=16)` for `one(20)`. Every kind of parameter, at its function's
// breakpoint, in gdb and lldb: scalars of every width; aggregates of 2 and
// 3 words (in registers) and of 5 (by a pointer); a borrowed struct that
// holds a string and a borrowed map (Place, a hidden pointer); a borrowed
// string and `[]T` (View); a `move []T`; named results (zero); an interface
// and an Option; value, pointer, Place and View receivers; the inlined
// copies of trivial functions (GIR inlining at `opt 0`) of each kind, and
// a View receiver inlined into its interface thunk; the thunk's frame shows
// nothing (artificial). The other side: after `next` the values are still
// right (xs grew, r was set), `break file:line` on a body line and on a
// declaration line (Doc.Count, line 79: the first line of its body) still
// work, and params-break-lines.test checks the line table on both targets.
//
// `step` into a function from a breakpoint by line in main (scalar, Place,
// View, named results, an inlined View): gdb's amd64 prologue analyser
// trusts the line table only for a producer that starts with "clang ", so
// it needs the frame pointer that `opt 0` with DWARF keeps (`push %rbp;
// mov %rsp,%rbp`) to go on to the end of the declaration line's row. Before
// the fix gdb stopped at the declaration line with wrong values; lldb
// stopped at the stores (the old prologue_end).
//
// GDB: Breakpoint 1, main.scalars (a=20, b=-7, c=true, f=2.5) at {{.*}}parambreak.gopp:32
// GDB: Breakpoint 2, main.words (p={X = 3, Y = 4}, t={A = 5, B = 6, C = 7}, g={A = 8, B = 9, C = 10, D = 11, E = 12}, k=13) at {{.*}}parambreak.gopp:37
